## Additional Issues Found During Code Analysis

---

### A — `regions` parameter inconsistency

The `regions` param is passed as a comma-delimited string (`'eu,uk,us'`) but the Odds API docs show it should be `regions=eu&regions=uk&regions=us` or `regions=eu,uk,us` — the comma-delimited form **is valid** per docs. No change needed.

---

### B — Profile Page is a Stub (Discovered, related to #7)

`app/profile/page.tsx` is 9 lines that say "Coming soon". This means clicking "Profile" in the nav goes to a blank page. Full implementation needed (same as issue #7 fix).

---

### C — Header Currency Select is Completely Disconnected

The `<select>` for currency in the header has no `onChange` handler, no state binding, and no connection to settings. Users who try to change currency via the header see nothing happen.

---

### D — `getMatchStatus()` Duration Assumptions are Wrong

Games are marked `finished` after 3 hours. But NFL games average 3.5h, baseball 3h+, and NHL overtime can reach 4h. This causes live games to disappear from the live feed.

---

### E — Betting Markets Tab Navigation in Match Detail Always Uses Mock Data

The `activeTab` variable in match detail controls which tab of `mockBettingMarkets` to display. Since all content is mocked Real Madrid data, every match shows the same markets regardless of the actual sport or event.

---

### F — No Error Boundary or Loading Fallback for Odds API Quota Exhaustion

If the Odds API quota is exhausted, the matches route returns a 500 error. The frontend shows "Aucun match trouvé" with no indication that the API quota is the problem. Add quota-exhaustion detection and a user-friendly message.

